  "title": "At Work in the Winter",
  "summary": "Winter in the vineyard doesn’t mean our crews take a break until spring — and the vines don’t either. It may look like little is happening during the dormancy phase, but beneath the surface, the vines have been working hard to tolerate and acclimate to the cold days of winter. After harvest, the vines’ roots […]",
